  {
   "id": "hippolyte",
   "name": "Hippolyte",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s17",
   "summary": "First mention: “Hippolyte, the groom from the inn, took the head of the horses from the coachman, and, limping along with his club-foot, led them to the door of the “Lion d’Or”, where a number of peasants collected to look at the car…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur",
   "name": "Monsieur",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s4",
   "summary": "First mention: “Monsieur and Madame Charles arrived at Tostes about six o’clock.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "berthe",
   "name": "Berthe",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s12",
   "summary": "First mention: “At last Emma remembered that at the château of Vaubyessard she had heard the Marchioness call a young lady Berthe; from that moment this name was chosen; and as old Rouault could not come, Monsieur Homais was requeste…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur-bournisien",
   "name": "Monsieur Bournisien",
   "aliases": [
    "Bournisien"
   ],
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s20",
   "summary": "First mention: “His zeal seemed successful, for the club-foot soon manifested a desire to go on a pilgrimage to Bon-Secours if he were cured; to which Monsieur Bournisien replied that he saw no objection; two precautions were better…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur-canivet",
   "name": "Monsieur Canivet",
   "aliases": [
    "Canivet"
   ],
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s20",
   "summary": "First mention: “It was all very well to vary the potions and change the poultices; the muscles each day rotted more and more; and at last Charles replied by an affirmative nod of the head when Mere Lefrancois, asked him if she could…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "lestiboudois",
   "name": "Lestiboudois",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s10",
   "summary": "First mention: ““You live on the dead, Lestiboudois!”"
  },
  {
   "id": "hivert",
   "name": "Hivert",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s10",
   "summary": "First mention: “But that dawdler, Hivert, doesn’t come!””"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur-guillaumin",
   "name": "Monsieur Guillaumin",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s11",
   "summary": "First mention: “As he was a good deal bored at Yonville, where he was a clerk at the notary’s, Monsieur Guillaumin, Monsieur Léon Dupuis (it was he who was the second habitue of the “Lion d’Or”) frequently put back his dinner-hour in…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur-tuvache",
   "name": "Monsieur Tuvache",
   "role": "minor",
   "group": "g-tuvache",
   "firstAppearance": "s12",
   "summary": "First mention: “Binet, a few shopkeepers, two or three publicans, the cure, and finally, Monsieur Tuvache, the mayor, with his two sons, rich, crabbed, obtuse persons, who farmed their own lands and had feasts among themselves, bigot…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "viscount",
   "name": "Viscount",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s8",
   "summary": "First mention: “One of the waltzers, however, who was familiarly called Viscount, and whose low cut waistcoat seemed moulded to his chest, came a second time to ask Madame Bovary to dance, assuring her that he would guide her, and th…”"
  },
  {
   "id": "madame-tuvache",
   "name": "Madame Tuvache",
   "role": "minor",
   "group": "g-tuvache",
   "firstAppearance": "s12",
   "summary": "First mention: “That same evening this was known in Yonville, and Madame Tuvache, the mayor’s wife, declared in the presence of her servant that “Madame Bovary was compromising herself.””"
  },
  {
   "id": "marquis",
   "name": "Marquis",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s7",
   "summary": "First mention: “But towards the end of September something extraordinary fell upon her life; she was invited by the Marquis d’Andervilliers to Vaubyessard.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "monsieur-boulanger",
   "name": "Monsieur Boulanger",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s16",
   "summary": "First mention: “Monsieur Boulanger introduced his man, who wanted to be bled because he felt “a tingling all over.””"
  },
  {
   "id": "vincart",
   "name": "Vincart",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s29",
   "summary": "First mention: “At last Lheureux explained that he had a very good friend, Vincart, a broker at Rouen, who would discount these four bills.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "government",
   "name": "Government",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s10",
   "summary": "First mention: “I, if I were the Government, I’d have the priests bled once a month.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "voltaire",
   "name": "Voltaire",
   "role": "minor",
   "firstAppearance": "s10",
   "summary": "First mention: “Mine is the God of Socrates, of Franklin, of Voltaire, and of Beranger!”"
  },
  {
